25,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems physical assets complicate our audits and reporting. Software is easier to track, but some software is a black box.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Our capacity for helping with hiring is very uneven. Some roles are easy to fill, others are a nightmare.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Shizue,,Our past successes suggest a pattern. Certain types of tooling are safer bets for exits than operational businesses.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Misaki,,We are burning through reserves faster than expected. We need assets that the bank actually values as security.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Shion,,"Deployment isn't always immediate. Depending on the sector, we could be waiting months before a customer even turns it on.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Misaki, does that mean we should avoid companies with high upfront hardware costs?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,I'm also worried about the board. We are stretched thin on software oversight.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Shizue,,I've noticed that some sectors hold their customers much better during price hikes than others.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"Exactly, Mizuki. If the credit line doesn't cover the asset type, we're solely responsible for the follow-on.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Shion,,"And if it's hardware, we risk supply chain gaps. If it's sensitive data, we risk security bottlenecks.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shion, so you're saying both hardware and specialized software have their own distinct delays?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree with Shion. We should avoid anything requiring specialized field crews or supervisors.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Shizue,,I think we should prioritize the models that have historically shown the most resilience in retention.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"I'm leaning toward something that doesn't require constant, unplanned capital injections.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Shion,,Precisely. I want a path to deployment that is predictable and fast.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"It sounds like we are all wary of operational complexity, whether it's in the audit or the field.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
